  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/bujurquina_oenolaemus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Bujurquina oenolaemus is a very pretty species of Bujurquina from Bolivia, described scientifically in 1987 by Kullander. The fish are biparental, larvophilous mouthbrooders. It reaches only 10-12 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/bujurquina_oenolaemus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: bred. Available size: 4-6 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/bujurquina_oenolaemus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping of this small jewel is possible in relatively small tanks of 100 l. If the fish are kept in larger tanks even a number of couples can be kept together.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/bujurquina_oenolaemus_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is very interesting to observe the interactions of such a group.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/bujurquina_oenolaemus_en/",
      "html": "<p>It took almost 20 years before the first living specimens were brought to Austria, Switzerland and Germany by travelling aquarists. Soon after, breeding was successful and so the species was spread in the hobby.</p>"
    }
  ],
